import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 867 | Transcended Ones and Society · Overview — The Transcended One's Social Responsibility","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 867 | Transcended Ones and Society · Overview — The Transcended One's Social Responsibility","no":867,"module":4,"tags":["Transcendence","Society","Social Responsibility","Myriad-Rank Republicanism","Civilizational Weight"],"related":["05-Myriad Ranks Joint Progress Basic Program","36-Social Structure and Class Mobility","706-Transcended One's Civilizational Weight","777-Transcended Ones and Myriad Ranks Overview"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0867_模块4-超脱者与社会-总论.md","filePath":"en/0867_模块4-超脱者与社会-总论.md"}`),o={name:"en/0867_模块4-超脱者与社会-总论.md"};function a(r,e,l,d,c,h){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="entry-867-transcended-ones-and-society-·-overview-—-the-transcended-one-s-social-responsibility" tabindex="-1">Entry 867 | Transcended Ones and Society · Overview — The Transcended One&#39;s Social Responsibility <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-867-transcended-ones-and-society-·-overview-—-the-transcended-one-s-social-responsibility" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 867 | Transcended Ones and Society · Overview — The Transcended One&#39;s Social Responsibility&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 05, 36, 706, 777</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-greater-the-power-the-heavier-the-social-responsibility-—-but-responsibility-is-not-grace" tabindex="-1">Introduction: the greater the power, the heavier the social responsibility — but responsibility is not grace <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-greater-the-power-the-heavier-the-social-responsibility-—-but-responsibility-is-not-grace" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: the greater the power, the heavier the social responsibility — but responsibility is not grace&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old world says &quot;the greater the ability, the greater the responsibility,&quot; which often degenerates into the strong one&#39;s self-moving: whom he wants to save he saves, whom he wants to punish he punishes; responsibility is defined by himself. Heng Yuan Zhou completely reverses this: <strong>the transcended one&#39;s social responsibility is not chosen by himself, but jointly defined by the civilizational-weight system, Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision, and Myriad-Rank-representative authorization.</strong> This entry is the &quot;Transcended Ones and Society&quot; sub-theme overview, answering one total question: what responsibility does the transcended one actually owe society, to whom, to what degree, and who assesses his fulfillment.</p><p>Six top-level axioms simultaneously take the stage: the anti-predation axiom requires responsibility not be discharged by predatory means; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires responsibility face all Myriad-Rank beings, not only the strong ones&#39; circle; the collective ascension axiom requires responsibility&#39;s landing point be lifting Myriad Ranks forward together; the causal self-discipline axiom requires the responsibility-discharge process be traceable and not disturb Myriad Ranks&#39; causality; the law-first axiom requires the social-responsibility system itself be a law-level self-consistent setting, infinitely scalable without setting-breaking; the universal equal infinite law confirms all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; easygoing layabouts retain a floor and are not eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher infinity — infinite origin is inherent in all, predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-the-transcended-one-s-three-layers-of-social-responsibility" tabindex="-1">I. The Transcended One&#39;s Three Layers of Social Responsibility <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-the-transcended-one-s-three-layers-of-social-responsibility" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. The Transcended One&#39;s Three Layers of Social Responsibility&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one&#39;s social responsibility is not a vague mass of &quot;doing good,&quot; but a law-anchored three-layer structure:</p><ol><li><strong>Bottom-line responsibility</strong>: do not predate, do not disturb the people, do not break Myriad Ranks&#39; symbiotic order. This is the minimum requirement; violation triggers the Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s red-line alert. Bottom-line responsibility corresponds to the anti-predation axiom&#39;s hard constraint.</li><li><strong>Post responsibility</strong>: as the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm officeholder, the transcended one must fulfill his legal post duties (law-network maintenance post, Myriad-Rank evolution-guidance post, cross-plane anchor-construction post, etc.; see entries 711–720). Post responsibility is the core of civilizational-weight assessment; doing poorly leads to demotion, rotation, even revocation of transcended-one qualification.</li><li><strong>Increment responsibility</strong>: the transcended one must proactively develop increments, create new resources, open new planes, leaving Myriad Ranks&#39; descendants a wider evolutionary space than when he took over. Increment responsibility corresponds to the collective ascension axiom — the strong do not ascend alone, but lift Myriad Ranks forward together.</li></ol><p>The three layers are indispensable. Only bottom-line without post is hang-up retirement; only post without increment is conservative stagnation; only increment without bottom-line may become &quot;under construction name, predation reality.&quot;</p><h2 id="ii-to-whom-is-the-transcended-one-responsible" tabindex="-1">II. To Whom Is the Transcended One Responsible <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-to-whom-is-the-transcended-one-responsible" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. To Whom Is the Transcended One Responsible&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old world&#39;s strong one is responsible to himself — my fate is mine, not heaven&#39;s. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s transcended one is responsible to four sides:</p><ul><li><strong>Responsible to Myriad-Rank beings</strong>: every decision he makes may affect billions of beings&#39; evolutionary path; therefore Myriad Ranks are his ultimate responsibility object;</li><li><strong>Responsible to the Anchor Council</strong>: the council represents Myriad Ranks in legislation, budgeting, and supervision; the transcended one must report post performance to it;</li><li><strong>Responsible to Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision</strong>: all behavior leaves traces, accepting algorithm and ethics-committee dual review;</li><li><strong>Responsible to future generations</strong>: increment responsibility&#39;s object is not only contemporaries, but also Myriad-Rank descendants not yet born — he may not exhaust stock and leave descendants no road.</li></ul><p>Four-side responsibility ensures the transcended one does not become an isolated sovereign &quot;responsible only to his own conscience.&quot; His conscience is unimportant; institutions are important.</p><h2 id="iii-how-social-responsibility-is-quantified" tabindex="-1">III. How Social Responsibility Is Quantified <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-how-social-responsibility-is-quantified" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. How Social Responsibility Is Quantified&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou does not engage in &quot;moral model&quot; style vague evaluation. The transcended one&#39;s social-responsibility fulfillment is quantified by the civilizational-weight system:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Responsibility Dimension</th><th>Quantification Indicator</th><th>Weight</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Power restraint</td><td>Energy-deployment records, no predation incidents</td><td>25%</td></tr><tr><td>Post contribution</td><td>Post-duty completion degree, Myriad-Rank benefit scale</td><td>30%</td></tr><tr><td>Increment development</td><td>New-resource / new-law / new-plane opening volume</td><td>25%</td></tr><tr><td>Social feedback</td><td>Education, medical, infrastructure investment</td><td>10%</td></tr><tr><td>Supervision cooperation</td><td>Alaya review cooperation degree, no concealment</td><td>10%</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Quantification is not to turn people into numbers, but to eliminate &quot;I feel I am already very responsible&quot; self-talk. Numbers do not lie, but numbers must be calibrated with Myriad-Rank representatives&#39; participation — this is the republican axiom of Myriad Races&#39; expression in responsibility assessment.</p><h2 id="iv-social-responsibility-and-the-transcended-one-s-personal-rights" tabindex="-1">IV. Social Responsibility and the Transcended One&#39;s Personal Rights <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-social-responsibility-and-the-transcended-one-s-personal-rights" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Social Responsibility and the Transcended One&#39;s Personal Rights&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Fulfilling social responsibility does not equal sacrificing personal rights. Heng Yuan Zhou insists: the transcended one is first a being, second a post officeholder. He has the right to rest, the right to personal cultivation, the right to choose rotation direction. Social-responsibility boundaries are drawn by law, not by moral kidnapping.</p><p>The old world&#39;s most insidious routine is &quot;you&#39;re so strong, what&#39;s wrong with helping me&quot; — alienating social responsibility into uncapped moral extortion. Heng Yuan Zhou refuses this extortion by institution: the transcended one&#39;s responsibility is legal post responsibility, not an on-call free nanny. He helps you because the post needs it; he does not help you also because the post needs it. Neither accepts moral trial.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the transcended one&#39;s energy must be used for social responsibility, not self-consumption or private grudges, eliminating waste of great talent on trivial tasks</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: responsibility discharge absolutely does not proceed by predatory means — one may not devour other civilizations &quot;to protect Myriad Ranks&quot;</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s responsibility is &quot;bearing all beings&#39; sins,&quot; defined and borne by him alone, ultimately lonely; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s transcended-one responsibility is defined by Myriad-Rank institutions, multi-party assessed, rotatable and perpetual</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: social responsibility faces all five-lineage Myriad-Rank beings, no favoritism, no omission</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: social-responsibility fulfillment records and assessment data open network-wide through the Selfless Dao, accepting Myriad-Rank supervision</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one&#39;s social responsibility is not grace, not self-moving, not moral kidnapping. It is a public institution anchored by laws, tracked by Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision, quantified by civilizational weight, and calibrated by Myriad-Rank representatives. The transcended one, because strong, therefore bears more; but what he bears, how much, and how well he does, is not for him to decide — for Myriad Ranks to decide. This is the transcended one&#39;s orthodox definition in the social dimension.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/05-万族共进基本纲领.html">Entry 05 · Myriad Ranks Joint Progress Basic Program</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/36-社会结构与阶层流动.html">Entry 36 · Social Structure and Class Mobility</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/706_模块4-超脱者的文明权重.html">Entry 706 · Transcended One&#39;s Civilizational Weight</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/777_模块4-超脱者与万族-总论.html">Entry 777 · Transcended Ones and Myriad Ranks Overview</a></li></ul>',27)])])}const y=i(o,[["render",a]]);export{p as __pageData,y as default};
